  "term": "MSH",
  "definition": "MSH stands for melanocyte-stimulating hormones, a group of peptides that act on pigment cells to promote melanin production and spread, leading to increased coloring of the skin and other tissues. These hormones come from pro-opiomelanocortin and are made in parts of the pituitary and in hypothalamic neurons.",
